# The recorded runs are data, read field by field with awk on every lane
# including the Windows ones. A checkout that turned them into CRLF would put a
# carriage return on the last field of every row -- which is a tick a reader
# cannot parse as a number, and an invisible difference in every reading derived
# from it. They are LF wherever they land.
*.tsv text eol=lf

# The suites and the launcher's own parts, for the same reason one step down:
# these are run by bash on Windows, and `\r` at the end of a line is a syntax
# error there in exactly the places it is hardest to read.
*.sh text eol=lf
